# Integration test configuration for go-filemaker.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is committed.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The integration suite (integration_test.go, build tag `integration`) reads
# these. Load them and run with:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   go test -tags=integration -run Integration -v ./...
# or: make integration

# Required ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Host, with or without scheme (https is assumed when omitted).
FM_HOST=https://fms.example.com

# Database name.
FM_DATABASE=MyDatabase

# Account credentials.
FM_USERNAME=apiuser
FM_PASSWORD=changeme

# A dedicated, disposable test layout — never production data. It must expose at
# least these Data API-editable fields: TextField (text), NumberField (number),
# TextSecondary (text), DateField (date), TimestampField (timestamp),
# TimeField (time), ContainerField (container), and RequiredField (text,
# validated Not Empty / "Validate always" / not user-overridable, so the host
# enforces it).
#
# The portal test also needs a second table, ChildTable, in a one-to-many
# relationship with ParentTable: a ChildText field shown in a portal on the
# layout, related on a match key. On the ChildTable side of the relationship,
# enable both "Allow creation of records in this table via this relationship" and
# "Delete related records in this table when a record is deleted in the other
# table". See integration_test.go for details.
#
# Tests self-clean via t.Cleanup, leaving the layout empty.
#
# FM_LAYOUT is the name of the layout to test against — the one built on the
# ParentTable table (named "ParentTable" in these instructions, but it can be
# any name; set FM_LAYOUT to whatever you called it).
FM_LAYOUT=ParentTable

# Optional ------------------------------------------------------------------

# IANA time zone used to interpret date/timestamp fields on read-back. When set,
# the WithLocation timestamp round-trip test runs; otherwise it skips. Every
# other test runs with the default location, UTC.
# FM_LOCATION=Europe/Stockholm

# Set to 1 to log every HTTP request/response to stderr (auth redacted) while the
# tests run. Handy for debugging a failure against the live host.
# FM_DEBUG=1

# Set to 1 to allow a plaintext http:// host (local development only).
# FM_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
